model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Account tool-call traffic follows committed per-account counter revisions in the saved account's existing owner scope. Only explicitly selected accounts that the current principal may inspect reach an organization stream or head receipt, with the same accountAccesses policy checked before and after current heads and before delivery. A private account's call changes no org-wide head or another member's feed and causes no read for that member. Bounded selectors preserve the 32-key protocol and at most two counter requests run concurrently. App details and user links retain authoritative mutation and permission handling while following their committed topics, with zero healthy idle body reads. Expired-hour purges add no traffic revision while deleting retained hours does. Normal hosted migration 23 adds the counter trigger without rewriting retained counts or depending on explicit journal activation 22. Legacy account-schema fixtures rewind the recorded migration suffix from the named account_changes step, including later IDs, before replaying the removed schema. Focus refresh targets the watched query so request failures remain visible and server-rendered reads retain serializability. A failed server fence hydrates the same typed failure without an unconfirmed body or invented receipt. Hover completes app and tool reads before opening without additional reads, even when the head check separates their batches. Revoking the parent login immediately evicts its protected app frame; scoped-session refusals preserve the document and draft."
    }
  }
}
